From 4ad58e7d2f9377edd71f0e8b81a02cfc4be8b83e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BellSoft <info@bell-sw.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:45:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vendor sources: a configured source is consulted in online
 scans

A source given with --vendor-url or --vendor-feed is used in every scan,
not only with --offline-vulnerabilities:

* In online scans the products it covers are matched by vulnmatch/osvlocal
  from the configured archives and left out of the vulnmatch/osvdev batch
  query (osvdev.Options.MatchedLocally). Without the options nothing
  changes.
* An unavailable configured archive is handled like a built-in default: a
  warning naming the source, and the scan continues; --vendor-strict fails
  the scan.
* A --vendor-url or feed naming a local location that does not exist is
  rejected before the scan (checkVendorOptions).
---
